From 66113b5f7432d39bfd88e6e9568bac4915a5d3a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom <tom@getimpala.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:09:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [Reload] Keep captured-graph tensors valid across
 reload_weights after a level-2 sleep (NVFP4 MoE + MLA)

Experiment 5 on an 8xB300 (Impala, 2026-10-11), GLM-5.2-NVFP4 (ModelOpt NVFP4 MoE on the FlashInfer
TRTLLM backend + MLA), vLLM 0.20.2. Sleep level 2 discards every allocation of the "weights" memory
pool. `reload_weights` refills parameters and buffers in place through the layerwise kernel-tensor
copy, but tensors DERIVED at load time and held as plain attributes are re-derived into NEW tensors
while the CUDA graphs keep the OLD pointers, whose memory was discarded: the fused-MoE quant
config's `a1_gscale`/`a2_gscale` (read by the captured input-quant kernel) and MLA's absorbed
`W_UV`/`W_UK_T` (read by the captured bmm). Eager steps use the new tensors, graph replays the
stale ones -> HTTP 200 with garbage tokens. Independently, `expand(num_experts)` made the
kernel-format MoE input scales stride-0 views, which Tensor.copy_ refuses as a destination
("more than one element of the written-to tensor refers to a single memory location").

Changes (behaviour gated by IMPALA_RELOAD_FIX=1; additive parts are always on):
- flashinfer_fp4_moe: shared input scales via `.repeat` (port of #49489).
- replace_parameter(prefer_copy=True): in-place refresh keeps data_ptr (port of #40390).
- MLA: W_UV / W_UK_T are parameters refreshed in place on reload (port of #48251).
- ModelOpt NVFP4 MoE: on a reload keep the MoE kernel the graphs were captured with and copy the
  freshly processed quant-config tensors into its live ones (no upstream equivalent as of
  2026-10-11: main still rebuilds the kernel, so its a1_gscale goes stale after a level-2 sleep).
- layerwise reload: overlap-tolerant kernel-tensor copy (defensive).
- Checksum hook v2 (IMPALA_WEIGHT_CHECKSUM=<dir>): parameters + buffers (Exp-4 digest) and derived
  tensors (module attributes, quant-config descriptors, experts attributes) with data_ptr, callable
  after wake_up + reload via /collective_rpc impala_weight_checksum.

